.TH KODISTILLER 1 "November 25, 2026" "Version 2026-11-25" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
kodistiller \- extract TVDB television series data for Kometa for import to Plex
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B buildtvdbyaml.sh
.br
.B python buildtvdbyaml.py
.RI [ series_id
.RI [ season_type
.RI [ edition_type ]]]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B kodistiller
extracts television series metadata from The TVDB v4 API and generates YAML
metadata files formatted for Kometa to import directly into a Plex database.
It consists of a POSIX-compliant shell wrapper
.RB ( buildtvdbyaml.sh )
that scans media directories for tagged series folders, and a Python generator
.RB ( buildtvdbyaml.py )
that queries the API and writes per-series YAML output files.
.PP
Because Plex ends data access contracts with The TVDB in December 2026,
.B kodistiller
provides an automated workaround for series whose metadata or episode ordering
from alternative sources is incomplete or inaccurate, without requiring local
NFO/JPG sidecar files or modifying embedded media tags.
.PP
.B kodistiller
retrieves series, season, and episode titles, summaries, first air dates,
series content ratings, and episode thumbnails. It does
.I not
populate genres, actors, studios, collections, episode ratings, or series and
season posters/artwork. Users should generally add new shows using TMDB metadata
first to fetch missing artwork and credits, and apply
.B kodistiller
where episode ordering or metadata requires TVDB data.
.PP
Note that Kometa cannot alter the episode ordering flag inside Plex for a
library or series; changing the episode order setting in Plex remains a manual
step.
.SH OPTIONS & ARGUMENTS
.B buildtvdbyaml.sh
takes no command-line flags; it is configured by editing variables at the top
of the script and scanning folder tags in
.IR MEDIA_PATH .
.PP
.B buildtvdbyaml.py
accepts up to three positional arguments:
.TP
.I series_id
Numeric TVDB series ID (defaults to
.B 121361
if omitted).
.TP
.I season_type
The TVDB API ordering string (defaults to
.BR default ).
Common values include:
.RS
.TP
.B default
Aired order (maps to
.B official
for season lookups).
.TP
.B official
Official aired order.
.TP
.B dvd
DVD release order.
.TP
.B absolute
Absolute episode numbering order.
.TP
.B alternate
Streaming or alternate order.
.TP
.B regional
Regional release order.
.TP
.B altdvd
Alternate DVD order.
.RE
.TP
.I edition_type
Optional Plex edition filter used to restrict metadata matching to a specific
edition (for split or multi-edition series).
.RS
.TP
.I <edition_name>
Matches only Plex items whose edition contains
.I <edition_name>
(generates
.BR edition_contains ).
.TP
.B none
Matches only the default edition lacking an edition tag (generates
.BR "blank_edition: \(dqtrue\(dq" ).
.TP
.I (omitted)
Applies metadata across all editions and split versions of the series.
.RE
.SH DIRECTORY TAGGING
When running
.BR buildtvdbyaml.sh ,
series directories under
.I MEDIA_PATH
are parsed using curly-brace tags in the directory name:
.TP
.BI {tvdb- digits }
Required. Specifies the numeric TVDB series ID.
.TP
.BI {tvdborder- order }
Optional. Specifies the TVDB API season ordering string (defaults to
.B default
if omitted).
.TP
.BI "{tvdborder-" "order edition" "}"
Optional. Specifies both the TVDB API season ordering string and an edition
filter separated by a space. Use
.B none
as the edition keyword to target only untagged default editions.
.SH CONFIGURATION
.SS Shell Script (buildtvdbyaml.sh)
Edit the path variables at the top of
.BR buildtvdbyaml.sh :
.TP
.B MEDIA_PATH
Root directory of your television library (default:
.IR /media/television ).
.TP
.B CONFIG_PATH
Target Kometa metadata directory where generated YAML files and logs are
written (default:
.IR /usr/local/share/kometa/config/metadata/Television/ ).
.SS Python Script (buildtvdbyaml.py)
Customize the configuration block at the top of
.BR buildtvdbyaml.py :
.TP
.B TVDB_API_KEY
Your TVDB v4 API key. Read automatically from
.I api.key
in the working directory if present, otherwise set directly in the script.
Never share your API key publicly.
.TP
.B TVDB_PIN
Subscriber PIN string if required by your TVDB API key (default:
.BR None ).
.TP
.B LANGUAGE
3-letter ISO 639-2 language code used to fetch localized series, season, and
episode titles and summaries when available (default:
.BR eng ).
.TP
.B COUNTRY
3-letter ISO country code used to select series content ratings (default:
.BR usa ).
.SS Kometa Configuration
Add the output directory to your Kometa configuration file under your TV
library:
.PP
.RS
.nf
TV Shows:
  metadata_files:
    - folder: config/metadata/Television
.fi
.RE
.SH FILES
.TP
.I ./api.key
Optional plain-text file containing your TVDB v4 API key.
.TP
.I tvdb_<SERIES_ID><EDITION>_metadata.yml
Generated Kometa metadata file written per series in the current working
directory. Each series is tagged with a Plex label formatted as
.BI tvdb- <season_type>
(for example,
.BR tvdb-dvd )
to identify TVDB-managed shows in the Plex UI.
.TP
.I serieslist.log
Deduplicated list of parsed series IDs, orders, and editions generated by
.BR buildtvdbyaml.sh .
.TP
.I run.log
Execution output log generated by
.BR buildtvdbyaml.sh .
.SH REQUIREMENTS
.IP \(bu 2
A Unix-like operating system (POSIX
.BR sh ,
.BR awk ,
.BR find ,
.BR sort ,
.BR tr ,
.BR xargs ). Windows compatibility is untested (may require Cygwin).
.IP \(bu 2
Python 3 with
.B tvdb_v4_official
and
.B PyYAML
installed
.RB ( "python -m pip install tvdb_v4_official PyYAML" ).
.IP \(bu 2
A working Kometa installation and a TVDB v4 developer API key.
.SH EXAMPLES
.TP
Scan all tagged folders in \fIMEDIA_PATH\fR and generate YAML files:
.B ./buildtvdbyaml.sh
.TP
Directory naming for DVD order:
.I /media/television/Firefly (2002) {tvdb-78874} {tvdborder-dvd}
.TP
Directory naming targeting only a specific Plex edition:
.I /media/television/Pokemon (1997) {tvdb-76703} {tvdborder-regional Japanese} {edition-Japanese}
.TP
Directory naming targeting only the untagged default edition:
.I /media/television/Pokemon (1997) {tvdb-76703} {tvdborder-official none}
.TP
Run manually from the command line for a single series (default aired order, all editions):
.B python buildtvdbyaml.py 76703
.TP
Run manually with a specific order across all editions:
.B python buildtvdbyaml.py 78874 dvd
.TP
Run manually for a specific order and Plex edition:
.B python buildtvdbyaml.py 76703 regional Japanese
.TP
Run manually for a specific order on the untagged default edition only:
.B python buildtvdbyaml.py 76703 official none
.SH KNOWN ISSUES & LIMITATIONS
.TP
.B Split or Multi-Edition Series Collisions
By default, generated YAML files match on TVDB ID across all editions or split
entries of a show (for example,
.I Pokemon (Aired in JP)
and
.IR "Pokemon (US Dub)" ).
If two folders share the same TVDB ID with different
.B {tvdborder-}
tags without edition specifiers, one ordering overwrites or applies to both.
Use Plex
.B {edition-}
tags paired with
.B "{tvdborder-<order> <edition>}"
(or
.BR none )
to isolate metadata per edition.
.TP
.B Partial Metadata Scope
Episode ratings, cast/crew, genres, studios, collections, and series/season
posters are not imported.
.TP
.B Disabled Dual-ID Matching
IMDB ID matching code is present in
.B buildtvdbyaml.py
as a fallback hedge against future Plex TVDB deprecations, but is currently
disabled by default.
